      "id": 1,
      "text": "Spring Valley was laid out in 1855 and named after a nearby spring that gave the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Valley%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Almanzo Wilder, husband of famed author Laura Ingalls Wilder, once farmed on land just outside Spring Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Valley%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Victorian‑Gothic Methodist Church, built in 1876, houses two floors of artifacts that chronicle the Wilders and local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://springvalleymnhistory.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Across the street from the church stands the Washburn‑Zittleman House and History Hall, preserving relics from yesteryear.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://springvalleymnhistory.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Spring Valley offers hunting, fishing, birding, hiking, and bike trails, plus an annual Wilder Fest in mid‑August.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.springvalley-mn.com/tourism",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A self‑guided walking tour highlights the historic downtown, antique shops, and the community’s preserved heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
